{"body":"Original unrestricted line-arrangement conjecture remains unsolved after five substantive turns. This draft preserves all 36 frozen author files and eight independent-review files, plus two additive publication guides.\n\nScoped results: an effective-coordinate finite-kernel algorithm when r<k²; the credited Hesse value with an auxiliary-line cover; all two-line extensions of supersolvable arrangements; Fermat deletion resilience; and an infinite 9q-line family with exact Seshadri constant 1/(4q+1). The source maximum is over all projective lines. The final dual proves only the component-cover optimum 4q, not optimality over arbitrary auxiliary lines.\n\nIndependent full scoped PASS: 214,070 author assertions and 93,918 independent controls replay exactly. Source report year2019 and publication date19November2020 are distinguished. Classical results are credited; no novelty or human peer-review claim.\n\nFresh main is first parent and frozen author WIP is second parent. Only this target folder and its own QUEUE status/turn cells changed. Python3 and SymPy are required. Public checkout replay passes with source_files_checked=0, explicitly omitting raw PDF/screenshot hashes; exact sources can be supplied separately. No raw source imports, private notes, merge or release.","headRefOid":"de6889b0ca34ceba9a08b85637272afe0b14af77","isDraft":true,"mergeCommit":null,"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":null,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/378"}
